A||N||6||Rumor||How to clean the doors and dash||||1||
Z||000000||Rumor||11-27-2001||02:44 AM||||My 85 had some dirt, ground-in gunk, scuff marks, and grime on the inner door panels and dash. I used a few art erasers( those rectangular ones) and a bunch of elbow grease, and WOW, the difference was amazing!  I'd suggest you use the white erasers.<BR>To finish it up, I used an "instant shine" sponge (impregnated with silicone) and it still looks shiny after three weeks, and it doesn't rub off on my fingers.  I bought the sponge for a buck.  I'll post the brand name tomorrow, when I find the box it came in. <BR>Hope this helps!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||11-27-2001||07:31 AM||||Another thing I've found to work on interior pieces is an S.O.S. pad.  Wet it, rub gently, and you'll be amazed at how well it will work.  You just have to make sure none of the blue goo from inside the pad drips onto the carpet.<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Frank Sombers||11-29-2001||07:33 PM||||Try KIWI saddle soap and an old toothbrush.<BR>Put some saddle soap on the brush, dip it into hot water and scrub the surface. Work up a lather and wipe off. Do a little area at a time. It goes slow but works great! It not only cleans but moisturizes the vinyl as well.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-29-2001||08:29 PM||||Don't scrub hard on the 2 tone dashs! You can scrub the color off on the painted section.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||11-29-2001||08:31 PM||||I use REN RP 70-S cleaner and a small scrub brush, then wipe the REN up with some paper toweling.  Old drimmy stuff comes out looking new, with no buff marks or scratches.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jake_Dragon||11-29-2001||09:01 PM||||KIWI sport shoe cleaner, works great.<BR>I bought the back part of the center console from a parts car that looked like it sat in the mud for the last 6 years, sprayed it down and wipe didn't even have to let it sit.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-29-2001||11:27 PM||||Once it's clean, for normal care and feeding, use 'Formula 2001' in the bright green spray bottle.  It's silicone based, and *will* protect your dash and replenish volitiles that evaporate out over the years.<P>Won't turn it brittle ever. Works great.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
